<title>RUSSIA: Russia 364-day T-bills yield 33.85 percent.</title>
<headline>Russia 364-day T-bills yield 33.85 percent.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of 364-day GKO discount Treasury bills (series 23004) was 33.85 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the annualised average yield for the bills would be 33.48 to 34.94 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the T-bill auction were as follows --</p>
<p>    Series number		   23004</p>
<p>    Issue volume		    6.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denomination		    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)		  8.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Bids (cash)		     6.20 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)		  5.99 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Proceeds			  4.48 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Average price		   74.76 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price	 74.55 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield		   33.85 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			     364 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		   April 8, 1998</p>
<p>Later on Wednesday the Finance Ministry will also auction four trillion roubles of an additional tranche of 119-day T-bills (series 22073).</p>
<p>It will pay 381.39 billion roubles in interest on the 18-month series 23005 OFZ interest-bearing government bond which matures in July 1997.</p>
<p>The ministry will also repay 6.29 trillion roubles in the series 22048 T-bills which mature on Wednesday.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
